// WITHDRAWN (2026-11-20, user-verified in-game on build 106): the page
// renders and persists (GameUserSettings.ini), but no script-reachable
// path applies the values to initial trader stock — with all three
// sliders set to 5.0 (persisted) a new game still seeded stock at the
// compile-time 3.0 values (Sharky ore 69, arrows 30). A HandleReadyForPlay
// CDO re-base of m_ItemsByDifficulty is too late / ineffective for initial
// stock. Kept for reference; do not enable without a working application
// path. See VALIDATION.md.

// RichMerchants — in-game settings page.
//
// Multipliers for every trader's ore / arrows / bolts stock. Values are
// applied at world start (and every save load) by URichMerchantsSubsystem
// (TraderStockRebase.as): the trader stock configs are re-based to exactly
// vanilla x value, so changing a setting takes effect from the next stock
// generation (chapter restocks, new games) — no restart needed for the
// config, but a load/new-game to apply.
//
// NOTE (build 106): only the `Value` member of FModUserSettingsFloat is
// script-bound (no DisplayText/MinValue/MaxValue/StepSize — those need a
// newer build), so the rows render with engine-default labels. Values are
// clamped to [0, 100] when applied.

UCLASS(Config = GameUserSettings)
class URichMerchantsUserSettings : UGothicModExt_UserSettings
{
    default CategoryName = FText::FromString("Rich Merchants");

    // NOTE: do NOT add `meta = (DisplayName = ...)` to these UPROPERTYs — a
    // frozen-main-menu-then-exit was observed on build 106 with it (the
    // ModExt settings scan appears to choke; reverted; see VALIDATION.md).
    // Slider order top->bottom = ore / arrows / bolts; build 106 binds no
    // DisplayText on FModUserSettingsFloat, so the rows render unlabeled.
    UPROPERTY(Config)
    FModUserSettingsFloat OreMultiplier = FModUserSettingsFloat(Value = 3.0f);

    UPROPERTY(Config)
    FModUserSettingsFloat ArrowMultiplier = FModUserSettingsFloat(Value = 3.0f);

    UPROPERTY(Config)
    FModUserSettingsFloat BoltMultiplier = FModUserSettingsFloat(Value = 3.0f);
}
